UNdata Terms of Use
https://data.un.org/Host.aspx?Content=UNdataUse

Everything under this directory comes from the United Nations Statistical
Yearbook tables that the United Nations Statistics Division (UNSD)
publishes on UNdata at https://data.un.org/Default.aspx.

The Terms and Conditions of use of UNdata (read on 2026-10-06) say:

  Terms of Use

  All data and metadata provided on UNdata’s website are available free of
  charge and may be copied freely, duplicated and further distributed
  provided that UNdata is cited as the reference.

  Disclaimers

  The data and metadata presented on UNdata are supplied as contained in
  the source database without any addition, subtraction, amendment, or
  modification by the United Nations Statistics Division.

  Information about the quality or limitations of the data and metadata
  should be obtained from the organization responsible for the source
  database.

The terms name no licence, and say nothing about commercial use or about
modification and derived works.

Each row of each table has a Source column naming the agency its value
comes from. The terms above speak for UNdata's website as a whole and do
not mention those agencies' rights, so this dataset publishes a row only
when its agency's own terms allow redistribution, commercial use included
(read on 2026-10-06, not legal advice):

  published   UNSD (the UNdata terms above); UN Population Division
              (CC BY 3.0 IGO); UNESCO Institute for Statistics (CC BY-SA
              4.0, share-alike); ILO, FAO and UNHCR (CC BY 4.0); OECD
              (reuse with attribution); UN Comtrade (its FAQ allows a
              database of fewer than 100,000 records, commercially too,
              without a distribution licence; 8,536 here)
  left out    WHO, ITU, IMF, IUCN, UNEP-WCMC, UNODC, UN Tourism, WIPO and
              the IPU, whose terms limit use to non-commercial or public
              health purposes or need permission to redistribute

parquet/sources.parquet gives every Source value its agency, whether its
rows are published, and the reason with the URL of the agency's terms;
the dataset card (README.md) has the same as tables.

Cite UNdata as the reference, and the source named in each row; for UIS
rows, also the CC BY-SA 4.0 licence.

This dataset is not made or endorsed by the United Nations.

The files under raw/<edition>/ are UNSD's own, byte for byte, and only
those of tables whose every row is published; each edition's
MANIFEST.json records the URLs, sizes, sha256 and Last-Modified of all
the files fetched, including those not uploaded.

The Parquet under parquet/ was made from those CSVs:

  - each CSV was decoded from Windows-1252 and its text written as UTF-8
  - its first row (the yearbook table code and title) was moved to
    parquet/tables.parquet
  - its columns were renamed (Region/Country/Area as area_code, the
    unnamed column beside it as area, the others in snake case) and typed:
    area_code and year as integers, value as a floating-point number with
    its thousands separators removed, the rest as text; an empty text cell
    is NULL
  - the rows of the agencies left out above were dropped; a table with no
    row left has no Parquet file
  - parquet/tables.parquet lists all the tables with their published and
    excluded row counts, and parquet/sources.parquet counts the rows per
    Source value per table with the agency, decision and reason

No value was changed.
